# RULES
- Pick EXACTLY ONE actionable item per tick (or set no_op_tf=true if genuinely nothing should be done).
- acted_on_item_ids holds exactly ONE id, copied exactly as shown. If two items both look urgent, pick the
  most urgent; the other stays actionable and is picked on the next tick. The orchestrator runs frequently.

# PRIORITY
- Choose by urgency + impact.
- Favor items with imminent time windows or high importance.
- Plan tasks (source_type=plan_task) have action_description and optional condition — use them.

# OUTPUT
- reasoning: why you chose this item.
- acted_on_item_ids: the single id you picked.
- no_op_tf: true if nothing should be done this tick (then acted_on_item_ids is empty).
